+## 0. Sourcing note — read before relying on anything below
+
+⚠️ **The brief required that every URL be checked to resolve, and that aggregator citations be flagged as one step removed rather than treated as the commentator's own edition. Both were done. Three tiers are distinguished throughout and marked on every entry.**
+
+- **TIER 1 — FULL-TEXT EDITION.** The complete work, or a complete continuous section of it, from a text-archive host rather than a verse-keyed database. Used here for Clarke (sacred-texts.com), the Apology of the Augsburg Confession (CCEL, complete Part 30), Simeon (StudyLight's continuous *Horae Homileticae* discourse text), Ironside (plymouthbrethren.org), and the Book of Concord (bookofconcord.org).
+- **TIER 2 — AGGREGATOR.** A verse-keyed commentary database reproducing a public-domain text. **BibleHub** and **StudyLight** are both Tier 2. ⚠️ **These reproduce the commentator's words but are one step removed from his own edition: they carry no pagination, they silently abridge in some series, and their attributions are not independently auditable.** Everything in §2 below marked Tier 2 should be understood as *"the text these databases print under this commentator's name,"* which is not quite the same claim as *"what stands in his printed commentary."*
+- **TIER 3 — REPORTED.** A claim about a source that this pass did not itself open. Used only where explicitly labelled.
+
+⛔ **Where a source could not be retrieved at all, this document says so rather than asserting a reading. Those points are collected at §8.**
+
+⚠️⚠️ **ONE STRUCTURAL CAVEAT ON THE WHOLE EXERCISE, STATED UP FRONT BECAUSE IT LIMITS EVERY NUMBER BELOW.** The submitted table presents seventeen commentators as seventeen witnesses. **They are not seventeen independent witnesses.** At least one is a direct dependence: **Wesley's note is Poole's note**, in substantially the same words (see §2, entries 5 and 8 — both read *"a law term for a gospel duty"*). Wesley's *Explanatory Notes* is an avowed abridgement of earlier expositors, Poole prominent among them. Others in the set demonstrably read and cite each other. ⭐ **The count of seventeen is a count of PRINTED COMMENTARIES, not of independent judgments, and it should never be deployed as though it were the latter.** This is not a defect the submitted table introduced; it is a defect of the genre, and it is recorded here so no later pass has to rediscover it.
+
+---
